        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Russian attacks kill 27 before deadline for ceasefire proposed by Kyiv Issued on: 07/05/2026 - 16:15 Russian attacks throughout eastern Ukraine killed at least 27 people on Tuesday, including 12 in one of the worst strikes so far this year, hours before a midnight deadline ushering in an open-ended ceasefire proposed by Kyiv. Russia announced a ceasefire ​for May 8 ‌to 9 to coincide with commemorations of the Soviet Union's victory over Nazi Germany in World War Two and ⁠a military parade in Moscow's Red Square. Ukraine, in response, announced a proposal for an open-ended ceasefire starting on Wednesday, urging Russia to reciprocate. World Cup 2026: FIFA under fire for ticket prices 07/05/2026 Israel says it killed Hezbollah commander in first strike on Beirut since ceasefire 07/05/2026 Israel's war priorities sidelined as Trump pushes toward a limited deal with Iran 07/05/2026 French aircraft carrier pre-positions for possible Hormuz mission 07/05/2026 War in the Middle East: Satellite imagery reveal scale of damage to US bases in Gulf 07/05/2026 Starmer under pressure: 'Many Labour MPs can’t see UK PM leading them into next general election' 07/05/2026 UK ⚽ Champions League: Paris fans celebrate reaching the final 07/05/2026 Sport DRC leader Tshisekedi hints at possible rule beyond second term amid eastern war 07/05/2026 France resumes genocide probe against Rwanda ex-president's widow 07/05/2026"
